      "text": "January 1-8, 2026 | Natural Disasters Summary \n\nJanuary 1, 2026\nSicily, Italy | Mount Etna eruption with lava flows in Valle del Bove\nSan Diego, USA | Flash floods after heavy rain, multiple water rescues\nÇatak, Turkey | Avalanches hit villages, one fatality, mass evacuations\nTacuarembó, Uruguay | Severe storm with hail, strong winds, power outages\nCórdoba, Argentina | Violent storm with hurricane-force winds, one death\n\nJanuary 2, 2026\nIrecê, Brazil | Urban flooding after intense rainfall\nGuerrero Coast, Mexico | M6.5 earthquake, fatalities and widespread damage\nSalta, Argentina | Torrential rain and large hail flooded cities\nBanten, Indonesia | Major flooding in Cilegon and Serang, mass evacuations\nVratsa, Bulgaria | Hurricane-force winds, fatalities and power outages\n\nJanuary 3, 2026\nYoussoufia, Morocco | River overflow caused residential flooding\nBursa, Turkey | Gale-force winds disrupted transport and daily life\nNorth Island, New Zealand | Severe storms with hail, lightning, waterspouts\nMarin County, USA | Coastal flooding from king tides and heavy rain\nPoções, Brazil | Flash flooding submerged streets and vehicles\n\nJanuary 4, 2026\nLazio, Italy | Tornado damaged residential areas near Rome\nTaroudant Province, Morocco | Severe storm caused floods and evacuations\nMálaga Province, Spain | River flooding forced evacuations\nSłupsk, Poland | Historic snowfall paralyzed transport\n\nJanuary 5, 2026\nNorth Sulawesi, Indonesia | Deadly mudflows after heavy rain\nPuerto Plata, Dominican Republic | Flooding in cities and resort areas\nChubut, Argentina | Large wildfire forced evacuations\nPonte de Lima, Portugal | Rare winter wildfire in mountainous terrain\nWestern Cape, South Africa | Major wildfire threatened coastal communities\n\nJanuary 6, 2026\nDurrës, Albania | Severe flooding, evacuations, schools closed\nGjakova, Kosovo | Rivers overflowed, homes flooded, evacuations\nShimane, Japan | Strong earthquake disrupted transport\nKrumovgrad, Bulgaria | Flash floods cut off villages\n\nJanuary 7, 2026\nOujda, Morocco | Rare snowfall after 25 years\nWest Halmahera, Indonesia | Floods and landslides killed residents\nDavao Oriental, Philippines | M6.7 offshore earthquake\n\nJanuary 8, 2026\nCebu City, Philippines | Landslide at landfill killed one, many trapped\nIstanbul, Turkey | Violent storm with hurricane-force winds\nBelarus | Powerful winter cyclone caused outages nationwide\n\n#ALLATRA #GlobalWeather #NaturalDisasters #ExtremeWeather #Floods #Earthquake #Storm #Wildfire #Avalanche #Volcano #ClimateEvents",
